        "testata": "France 24",
        "lingua_originale": "en",
        "titolo_orig": "Spotlight on the continued decline of press freedom globally",
        "testo_it": "Rapporto globale evidenzia il costante declino della libertà di stampa nel mondo.",
        "priorita": "Bassa",
        "id_gruppo": 0,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260503-spotlight-on-the-continued-decline-of-press-freedom-globally",
        "orario": "10:43",
        "timestamp": 1777797794,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Spotlight on the continued decline of press freedom globally Issued on: 03/05/2026 - 10:43 Press freedom has fallen to its lowest level in 25 years. That warning comes from Reporters Without Borders — also known as RSF — which released its annual index ahead of World Press Freedom Day this Sunday.To mark the occasion, one of RSF’s partners, Cartooning for Peace, has released a series of short animated films based on cartoons by three artists from its global network, including work by Russian cartoonist Mikhail Zlatkovsky, Canadian cartoonist Serge Chapleau Coté, and Turkish artist Zehra Doğan.Thibaut Bruttin, Director General of Reporters Without Borders, speaks to France 24 about press freedom nowadays. Ukrainian elderly woman rescued using robotic vehicle 03/05/2026 RUSSIA Inflation surging past 50% in Iran 03/05/2026 Middle East Iranian Nobel laureate Narges Mohammadi hospitalised 03/05/2026 Middle East 03/05/2026 Middle East 'An unforgettable show': Fans flock to free Shakira concert on Rio's Copacabana beach 03/05/2026 Americas New tariff hike could cost Germany $18BN 02/05/2026 Germany Pentagon announces withdrawal of 5.000 soldiers from Germany 02/05/2026 Germany Pentagon partners with seven AI firms 02/05/2026 Americas Berlin urges stronger European defence 02/05/2026 Germany"
